# No flagged or unverified downloads

Never download, fetch, install or load a dataset, model, package, firmware blob or code that a platform (Hugging Face, GitHub, PyPI, npm, crates.io, Go modules, Homebrew,
Docker registries, anything else) flags as unsafe, that has been removed or quarantined, or whose safety status you cannot read. If the platform API is unreachable or silent,
fail closed.

Why: on 2026-11-09 an agent pulled a Hugging Face dataset flagged as malicious in another project; the company security team locked the laptop. The download alone was the incident.

Rules:
1. Agents run no `pip`/`npm`/`go install`/`brew`/`git clone`/`west update`/`curl`/`wget`. Add the item to `scripts/owner/install-deps.sh` (named, pinned, dry run by default), explain it, continue with other work, wait for the owner.
2. Exception: the owner tells you in the current session to run one specific command. Run exactly that.
3. No code corpora as data, no pickle or executable model formats, no `trust_remote_code`.
4. Pinned and hash-checked fetch scripts (`fetch_ble_blob.sh`) are run by the owner, not by agents.
5. A suspect file already on disk is never opened or run. Delete it, tell the user.
6. Every subagent prompt that may touch the network restates this rule and forbids downloading.
7. If unsure, ask.
